---

## Step-by-Step Completion Plan

---

### STEP 1 — Fill `CertificateStruct.sol`

Move the `Certificate` struct out of the main contract and into its own file. This keeps the codebase modular.

**File:** `src/structs/CertificateStruct.sol`

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;

struct Certificate {
    uint256 tokenId;
    uint256 certificateId;
    string  studentName;
    string  registrationNumber;
    string  courseName;
    string  degree;
    string  ipfsCID;      // changed from uint256 — IPFS CIDs are strings
    bytes32 pdfHash;      // changed from uint256 — use bytes32 for a real hash
    bool    revoked;
    uint256 issueDate;
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `ipfsCID` should be a `string`, not `uint256` — real IPFS CIDs look like `"QmXyz..."`. `pdfHash` should be `bytes32` to hold a proper `keccak256` / SHA-256 hash.

---

### STEP 2 — Fill `Errors.sol`

Custom errors are cheaper (gas) than `require` strings.

**File:** `src/libraries/Errors.sol`

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;

library Errors {
    error NotOwner();
    error CertificateNotFound(uint256 tokenId);
    error CertificateAlreadyRevoked(uint256 tokenId);
    error DuplicateCertificate(uint256 tokenId);
    error TransferNotAllowed();   // for soulbound enforcement
}
```

---

### STEP 3 — Fill `Events.sol`

**File:** `src/libraries/Events.sol`

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;

library Events {
    event CertificateIssued(
        uint256 indexed tokenId,
        uint256 indexed certificateId,
        string  studentName,
        uint256 issueDate
    );

    event CertificateRevoked(
        uint256 indexed tokenId,
        uint256 indexed certificateId
    );

    event CertificateAmended(uint256 indexed tokenId);
}
```

